---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Attribution from '../components/site/Attribution.astro';
import { CITATION, MANUAL } from '../data/citation';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<BaseLayout title="Sources" section="about" description="Sources, required attribution and content-use rules.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Sources</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="src-section" aria-labelledby="primary">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 id="primary">Primary source</h2></div>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          The curriculum follows <cite>{MANUAL.title}</cite> by {MANUAL.authors.join(', ')} ({MANUAL.institution}). It determines the
          C++ knowledge taught here, the order of concepts, and the four modelling destinations.
        </p>
        <div class="key"><Attribution label="Required attribution" /></div>
        <p>
          C++ Atlas is an independent educational project. It is not an official University of Groningen course and is not endorsed
          by the University of Groningen or the manual’s authors. All lesson text, examples, figures, laboratories and exercises are
          written independently.
        </p>
        <h3>What is not reproduced</h3>
        <p>
          The manual’s exercises, their solutions, the weekly programming assignments, the project specifications and their solutions
          are not published here, nor are modified versions of them. The manual’s own example programs and biological examples are not
          reused either; the site uses its own models (Beverton-Holt, host-parasitoid, a three-stage plant, logistic, elimination and
          SIR equations, birth-death and SIR Gillespie processes, and a spatial plant IBM).
        </p>
        <h3>Where this site corrects or updates the manual</h3>
        <p>
          Where the manual describes behaviour that is outdated or incorrect for modern C++, lessons teach the current behaviour and
          say so. Examples: <code>std::vector&lt;T&gt;(n)</code> value-initialises its elements; signed integer overflow is undefined
          behaviour; integer division truncates toward zero on every compiler since C++11; whether plain <code>char</code> is signed is
          implementation-defined; exceptions are caught by <code>const&amp;</code> and live in <code>&lt;stdexcept&gt;</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="src-section" aria-labelledby="supporting">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 id="supporting">Supporting sources</h2></div>
      <ul class="measure">
        <li><cite>Mastering Modern C++23: A Complete Guide to the Latest Standard</cite>: used selectively for modern syntax, safer idioms and compiler-support notes. The site keeps C++17 as its baseline and labels newer features.</li>
        <li><cite>Modern C++ in the Real World</cite>: used for software-engineering practice relevant to scientific models (organisation, testing, debugging, profiling, reproducibility).</li>
        <li><a href="https://en.cppreference.com/">cppreference.com</a>: the reference for language and library behaviour.</li>
        <li><a href="https://akaminas.github.io/vellum/">Vellum</a>: the design system for colour, typography and every scientific figure (MIT-licensed code; tokens copied verbatim).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="src-section" aria-labelledby="licences">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 id="licences">Licences</h2></div>
      <ul class="measure">
        <li>Vellum tokens and code: MIT licence, © 2026 Alexandros Kaminas.</li>
        <li>
          Fonts, self-hosted: Source Sans Pro (<a href={url('/fonts/OFL-SourceSans.txt')}>SIL Open Font License 1.1</a>) and Source Code Pro
          (<a href={url('/fonts/OFL-SourceCode.txt')}>SIL Open Font License 1.1</a>) on most pages; TeX Gyre Pagella
          (<a href={url('/fonts/GUST-FONT-LICENSE.txt')}>GUST Font License</a>) and Lato (<a href={url('/fonts/OFL-Lato.txt')}>SIL Open Font License 1.1</a>)
          on the landing page and the atlas.
        </li>
        <li>Course manual: {CITATION}. Its content is not redistributed.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .src-section { margin-top: 56px; }
  .src-section h3 { margin-top: 1.4em; }
</style>
